      "rationale": "As a busy parent juggling multiple responsibilities, I'd want to test the free tier first to confirm it actually solves the calendar fragmentation problem before committing financially. Once I see real time savings and reduced stress, the $6.99/month Plus tier becomes an easy upgrade.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "The email parsing in Pro is nice-to-have, but Plus covers the core need (6 members, digest, handoffs). After using Plus for a month or two and seeing consistent value, I might upgrade to Pro for the automation, but Plus is the natural starting point.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_monthly_cancel_anytime",
      "rationale": "I prefer flexibility—monthly billing lets me cancel if life changes or the app stops fitting our routine. With two kids and shifting schedules, I don't want to be locked into annual prepayment early on.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 first month is low-friction enough to test Plus features without guilt. I'll try it, but I'll cancel immediately if it doesn't demonstrably reduce the chaos of juggling school notices and activity pickups.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm pragmatic about tools—I'll compare FocusLoop against what my friend recommends, but I won't hunt endlessly for free alternatives. If one clearly wins on family coordination, I'll pay. Time is more valuable than a few dollars.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads are annoying but not a dealbreaker on free. I'd only pay to remove them if Plus itself is already solving my calendar problem—the ad-free experience is a bonus, not the reason to upgrade.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99/month for Plus, the pricing is reasonable if it actually eliminates the back-and-forth texting and missed deadlines. It's not cheap, but it's fair for the time and stress it saves a dual-income household.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
